{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1460486-create-a-hybrid-setting-trinity-continuum-40-000","id":1460486,"title":"Create-a-Hybrid-Setting: Trinity Continuum 40,000","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-19T18:23:12-07:00","id":1460486,"title":"Create-a-Hybrid-Setting: Trinity Continuum 40,000","content":"(repost from RPGnet...)<br /> <br /> <i>It is the 41st Millennium. For more than a hundred centuries the Proxies have sat immobile in the Aeon Council of Earth. They are the Masters of Mankind by the will of the gods, and master of a million worlds by the might of their inexhaustible armies. They are mummified carcasses writhing invisibly with power from the Dark Age of Quantum. They are the Carrion Lords of the Imperium for whom a hundred souls are sacrificed every day, so that they may never truly die.<br /> <br /> Yet even in their deathless state, the Proxies continue their eternal vigilance. Mighty battlefleets cross the twisting, hostile pseudo-reality of the Warp, the only route between distant stars, their way lit by the Astronomican, the psychic manifestation of their will. Vast armies give battle in their name on uncounted worlds. Greatest amongst their soldiers are the Legions, the Space Marines, telekinetically-empowered warrior-mystics. Their comrades in arms are legion: the Federal Army and countless planetary defense forces, the ever vigilant Ministry and the bio-sages of the Norca and \u00c6sculapian Order to name only a few. But for all their multitudes, they are barely enough to hold off the ever-present threat from madmen, warlords, mutants - and worse.<br /> <br /> To be a man in such times is to be one amongst untold billions. It is to live in the dying remnants of a dream of a better cosmos. These are the tales of those times. Forget the power of technology and science, for so much has been forgotten, possibly never to be re-learned. Forget the promise of progress and understanding, for in the grim dark future all pales before survival against a hostile cosmos. There is no peace amongst the stars in this era, only a seemingly-endless cavalcade of carnage and tragedy, and the laughter of scheming gods.<br /> <br /> But perhaps, one day, the era will end...</i><br /> <br /> [/obligatory]<br /> <br /> Hokay. How I got here deserves explanation...<br /> <br /> See, I had a lovely idea for a scene in one of my fics/adventure ideas in Chronicles of Darkness where the main characters enter a bubble of warped time, and as they explore, they enter moments of atrocity and oppression throughout past and future history, including the distant, stellar future, and encounter a group of alien survivors of a human warlord's massacre, who confuse them for soldiers of said warlord and attack. However, I wanted to show said aliens were alien, so I made them Chromatics from Trinity, and to convey the feel of &quot;dark side of the far future&quot;, so I raided art of the Adeptus Mechanicus for ideas.<br /> <br /> Somehow, this led to me wondering what the Trinity factions would be if they were...Warhammerized, and then led to me internally coming up with that spiel - what would happen if you crossbred two settings on very distant places on the optimism spectrum together, and found a medium?<br /> <br /> Yes, this is an uneasy and incompatible mix. I don't care, it's fun as hell to see the car crash of themes.<br /> <br /> I, obviously, can't, and won't, do that alone. But I did realize that, if you averaged out the settings, you'd have a big theme of &quot;low point of human existence&quot; - things can get better, and in time, probably will, but they can certainly get worse as well, and it's going to be long, hard, and unrewarding work. Kind of like Grim Hollow (5e third-party setting) In Space. Which also means that no, there is no rampant and unstoppable xenophobia on all sides, but everyone has a villainous faction that thinks there should be (thus, the endless war is not &quot;humans vs. daemons vs. aliens vs. different humans vs. entropy&quot;, it's 'everyone who does not think of their enemies as just meat vs. everyone who does vs hapless soldiers brought along for the ride vs mindless menaces that are echoes of previous tragedies&quot;).<br /> <br /> Also, I had the Coalition as the local equivalent of both Genestealer Cults and Dark Eldar; they invade and illegally modify people into unknowing slaves so they can abduct entire planetary populations to take back to their World-Ark, and rip apart entire species at a time to harvest their genetic distinctions to make better slaves. The 2E Coalition, mind you; there's a bit of dominance play, torture, and decadence going on, but it's not overtly sexual, but the focus is on how utterly terrible pastiches of aristocrats the Progenitors are, the horror of being treated as raw material for an endlessly gluttonous empire wherein your very flesh is a tool they will mutilate into forms pleasing to them, and how their servant phyles try to remain sane despite the oppression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 09-20-2021, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T09:35:43-07:00","id":1460545,"title":"","content":"Themes of sacrifice would be appropriate for both sources. Teams of \u201cInquisitives\u201d or \u201cQuaestors\u201d would have room for all sorts of Contiuum types. Also like a \u201call the bad is happening Right Now, but we have people who can make a difference \u201c . What kind of scale would you think? Street level hive city/lower deck crew on a Rogue Trader ship, Rogue Trader/Inquisitor and Friends, something in between?<br /> <br /> Assassin: Talent, with cyber or biokinetic mods, and telepathy-mindsculpting, details depending on the ordo. Maybe in the Ad Mech equivalent have more of a schism between bio and electro \u201ccyber\u201d (forget the exact terms for Nova computer vs psychich biomcomputer).<br /> <br /> High level psykers, exceptional space marines (and Primarchs if you use them, and maybe high end Ad Mech), are where Continum rule choices get important. Take the Nova power set, but more limits on only getting powers appropriate to your theme, maybe? Intellect and technocontrol for AM, mostly mega-attributes for SM, energy blast and other weird but themed powers for psykers. They all have the superhuman but turning trans or inhuman thing going on. Also, give lots of \u201cturn that failure into a botch in exchange for momentum\u201d type bargains so the players help show just how dangerous Psychic side effects can be.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d suggest Eldar, Sisters of B, Gray Kniggghts, low end psykers as Trinity Psion type characters. Less flashy powers, but less vulnerable to Warp Shenanigans, more team oriented, etc<br /> <br /> Rogue Traders as talents all the way. But with Plasma Guns.<br /> <br /> Tyranids &amp; genesteaker cults would map well to the collective hivemind type Aberrants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T09:46:26-07:00","id":1460547,"title":"","content":"I think it's possible that, if this is taking place over the span of millennia like in 40k, that the Proxies are probably past Psi 7 at this point, especially after getting fed hundreds of souls a day. Maybe even Psi 10? Not sure about that.<br /> <br /> Regardless, there's a few points in your narration where you still kept &quot;His&quot; rather than any plural pronouns. Not sure if you were really worried about consistency there or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T09:54:16-07:00","id":1460548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1460486-create-a-hybrid-setting-trinity-continuum-40-000?p=1460547#post1460547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, there's a few points in your narration where you still kept &quot;His&quot; rather than any plural pronouns. Not sure if you were really worried about consistency there or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed that too. My first guess was the Quantakin or Telepath Proxy was a He, as those are the powers I\u2019d associate with \u201cpsychic beacon in the warp\u201d. All Proxies permanently telepathiccaly linked would make sense as Emperor-analog, but my preference would be It or They pronouns in that case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T12:06:21-07:00","id":1460564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1460486-create-a-hybrid-setting-trinity-continuum-40-000?p=1460547#post1460547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, there's a few points in your narration where you still kept &quot;His&quot; rather than any plural pronouns. Not sure if you were really worried about consistency there or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, it's because I copy-pasted the narration, and find-replaced. Those were things I missed. Thanks for finding them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T14:35:43-07:00","id":1460580,"title":"","content":"This is a ton of fun. Cheers for going straight to the Hammer and not going Hammer-lite with StarCraft... <br /> <br /> If you wanted to go even more grim dark, all of the Orders could constitute legions - either chapters or occupations (ie Aescupalians could be Apothecaries). Psiads are viewed with extreme prejudice as the empire has built giant fortress planets to defend the tanks. Aberrants (and their sub-species) are similar to some chaotic elder gods - inscrutable and truly alien with glimpses of the familiar. <br /> <br /> The bloodlust gamers would love having the suite of powers at their disposal beyond the absurd weapons and bio-armor. The Rogue Trader guys could have a ton of fun with Talents and the aforementioned Psiad (it's an episode of Firefly that writes itself). <br /> <br /> May your plasma swords burn bright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T08:16:53-07:00","id":1460844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queen Anne Country</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1460486-create-a-hybrid-setting-trinity-continuum-40-000?p=1460580#post1460580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a ton of fun. Cheers for going straight to the Hammer and not going Hammer-lite with StarCraft... <br /> <br /> If you wanted to go even more grim dark, all of the Orders could constitute legions - either chapters or occupations (ie Aescupalians could be Apothecaries). Psiads are viewed with extreme prejudice as the empire has built giant fortress planets to defend the tanks. Aberrants (and their sub-species) are similar to some chaotic elder gods - inscrutable and truly alien with glimpses of the familiar. <br /> <br /> The bloodlust gamers would love having the suite of powers at their disposal beyond the absurd weapons and bio-armor. The Rogue Trader guys could have a ton of fun with Talents and the aforementioned Psiad (it's an episode of Firefly that writes itself). <br /> <br /> May your plasma swords burn bright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! And yeah, I feel the real core of Warhammer is scope - what Starcraft did really didn't get across the same level of epic at all. Nor the operatic tone and destructive spectacle of real grimdark (in my view of the genre). While I'm not aiming for the overwhelming bleakness of 40k (not only am I not capable of that, it'd suffocate the other half of the hybrid), but there's a lot of room that still remains properly grim and cynical. After all, I'm aiming for humanity's greatest achievement being a failing state.<br /> <br /> Very good suggestions too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T18:03:09-07:00","id":1460944,"title":"","content":"Another question, did you have a specific era in mind? Cause this would only be gane-relevant in the right time period\u2026<br /> <br /> What do you map to the Horus Heresy/Gods of Chaos, and to Vandire/age of Apostasy? Thematically, Chaos is an out of context problem to any rank below Emperor - some weird artifacts and races you conquer, then you find allies, who gradually twist and corrupt you, all because the boss tried to prevent you from knowing Chaos could exist. Classically, Aberrants and Doyen are kind of known threats, so fit the corruption but not the out of context. But wasn\u2019t there that \u201carc ship of many types of aliens, who are actually gengineered supspecies of a few masters?\u201d Or maybe borrow the ameoboid of unknown goals aliens from Eclipse Phase.<br /> <br /> And the Age of Apostasy seems like a good time for Trinity - empire taken over by one person/group, possibly insane or being controlled by a hidden party (Doyen, good for all your conspiracy needs, or a time traveler solving future problems in bad ways) with the Sebastian Thor-analog PC group as the ones who uncover the conspiracy, then need to find enough allies in high places to bring down the baddy and start a new improved era of the Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T20:24:41-07:00","id":1460975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1460486-create-a-hybrid-setting-trinity-continuum-40-000?p=1460944#post1460944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, did you have a specific era in mind? Cause this would only be gane-relevant in the right time period\u2026<br /> <br /> What do you map to the Horus Heresy/Gods of Chaos, and to Vandire/age of Apostasy? Thematically, Chaos is an out of context problem to any rank below Emperor - some weird artifacts and races you conquer, then you find allies, who gradually twist and corrupt you, all because the boss tried to prevent you from knowing Chaos could exist. Classically, Aberrants and Doyen are kind of known threats, so fit the corruption but not the out of context. But wasn\u2019t there that \u201carc ship of many types of aliens, who are actually gengineered supspecies of a few masters?\u201d Or maybe borrow the ameoboid of unknown goals aliens from Eclipse Phase.<br /> <br /> And the Age of Apostasy seems like a good time for Trinity - empire taken over by one person/group, possibly insane or being controlled by a hidden party (Doyen, good for all your conspiracy needs, or a time traveler solving future problems in bad ways) with the Sebastian Thor-analog PC group as the ones who uncover the conspiracy, then need to find enough allies in high places to bring down the baddy and start a new improved era of the Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Age of Apostasy sounds good - since that's the most conceivable time to set the Empire on a better course of some kind.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I had Doyen as the &quot;Hidden Archenemy&quot;; they're what I had in mind for &quot;scheming gods.&quot; They <i>want </i>everything to get worse, to avoid the risk of other ascendant species becoming a rival. Which makes them sort of both Chaos and the Old Ones here.<br /> <br /> Their ground forces are based on the Breach of From Alien Skies - they try not to make appearances in person, but they're fine yanking machines from higher dimensions and corrupting the world into guard posts against risks to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}